{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782914918,"nonce":"4tie1s8XF9m/Yh4RIB2OBjWY0eI=","title":"Validate the pinned-weight auto-budget end to end on a real Krea2 run. Built and unit-tested (93 tests) but never GPU/live-tested.","message":"What was built:\n- ModelConfig.layer_offloading_pinned_weight_gb (default -1 = auto: pin the whole offloaded/streamed weight set, capped by total RAM minus a floor; 0 = pin nothing; \u003e0 = manual GiB).\n- Pinned-source bypass in _stage_forward_weight: skip the pageable-\u003epinned worker copy when the source param is already pinned, so workers idle instead of pegging CPU.\n- promote_layer now returns freed pinned budget (fixed a counter leak across promote/demote cycles).\n\nWhy:\nThe bounce-pool workers were pegging ~1.4 cores doing pageable-\u003epinned copies (copy ~15.6 s/step @ 4.34 GB/s), lagging the whole machine on non-dedicated systems. Pinning the already-resident offloaded weights is ~RAM-neutral and should let workers idle.\n\nEvidence wanted:\n- bounce-pool copy GB/s up, copy_s down, worker_fills near zero (scripts/digest_perf_log.py).\n- Noticeably less system lag during training.\n- No RAM blowup (auto cap by total RAM minus floor respected).\n\nNote: no plan doc - context is in memory only. Block streaming (a696018) chased transfer COUNT; this chases the intrinsic copy cost, fixed by pinning not coalescing.","files":null}]}